## Mathematical Model

The system follows the closure principle: S = Closure(A, D) = ∪_{k=0}^∞ D^{(k)}(A)

Where:
- A = entry execution node
- D = dependency expansion operator
- S = complete system (canonical tree)

This mathematical model ensures all dependencies are properly resolved and the system remains consistent.